---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProductShowcase from '../../components/sections/ProductShowcase.astro';
import ProjectDiagram from '../../components/sections/ProjectDiagram.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="BajuTech Commerce — AI-Integrated E-Commerce Platform | Abu Sayaf"
  description="A production multi-tenant e‑commerce platform engineered with AI-integrated order intelligence, inventory orchestration, and automated courier logistics."
>
  <article class="article-page container">
    <a href="/#work" class="article-back">← Back to selected systems</a>
    <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:35px">SYSTEM CASE STUDY / 01</p>
    <h1>BajuTech Commerce — AI-Integrated E-Commerce Platform</h1>
    <p class="article-intro">
      A unified, high-throughput commerce platform engineered for omnichannel retailers and social-commerce operators — integrating automated order pipelines, real-time inventory synchronization, and logistics intelligence into one resilient engine.
    </p>
    <div class="article-meta">
      <span>Full-stack</span>
      <span>Multi-tenant architecture</span>
      <span>Cloud deployment</span>
      <span>Order management</span>
      <span>F‑Commerce / Social commerce</span>
    </div>

    <h2>Product in action</h2>
    <ProductShowcase kind="commerce" />

    <h2>The problem</h2>
    <p>
      Online and social‑commerce sellers operate across multiple channels simultaneously — websites, Facebook pages, and offline stores. Without a unified system, orders fall through the cracks, inventory data grows stale, and courier handoffs require tedious manual re‑entry. The result is missed sales, customer frustration, and unscalable operations.
    </p>

    <h2>System boundaries</h2>
    <div class="case-diagram"><ProjectDiagram kind="commerce" /></div>
    <p>
      This diagram illustrates the major responsibility boundaries. Each box represents a logical ownership domain — not necessarily a separate deployable microservice.
    </p>

    <h2>Core capabilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Centralised order management.</strong> Consolidates orders from social pages, online storefronts, and offline channels into a single workflow — statuses move from pending → processing → shipped → delivered with no manual re‑entry.</li>
      <li><strong>Catalogue & product management.</strong> Add, edit, and organise product listings, variants, pricing, and stock descriptions. Changes propagate instantly across all connected storefronts.</li>
      <li><strong>Real‑time inventory tracking.</strong> Stock levels update as orders are confirmed, preventing overselling and triggering low‑stock alerts before supply runs out.</li>
      <li><strong>Courier & logistics integration.</strong> Automates parcel hand‑off data to delivery partners, eliminating duplicate entry and reducing missed shipments.</li>
      <li><strong>Hybrid online + offline operations.</strong> Syncs digital storefronts with traditional offline sales channels, giving merchants one dashboard for the entire business.</li>
      <li><strong>Mobile‑optimised dashboards.</strong> Merchants manage their full workflow from any device, with responsive UI that surfaces the most important actions first.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The decisions that matter</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tenant isolation.</strong> Every merchant's data, order streams, and inventory are strictly scoped to their own context — shared infrastructure, isolated state.</li>
      <li><strong>Order state machine.</strong> Explicit, auditable transitions prevent orders from being skipped, double‑processed, or silently lost.</li>
      <li><strong>Idempotent courier calls.</strong> External logistics APIs are called with idempotency keys so network retries never duplicate shipments.</li>
      <li><strong>Observability first.</strong> Every order event, state change, and stock mutation is logged with enough context to reconstruct exactly what happened and why.</li>
      <li><strong>Maintainability over micro‑services.</strong> Components are split along ownership boundaries and coupling, not for the sake of a distributed‑systems aesthetic.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="article-panel">
      <p><strong>Live platform:</strong> <a href="https://commerce.bajutech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">commerce.bajutech.com</a> — a production system serving real merchants across online and social‑commerce channels.</p>
    </div>

    <a href="https://commerce.bajutech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="button button--primary" style="margin-right:12px">View live platform ↗</a>
    <a href="/#book" class="button button--primary">Book a meeting ↗</a>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
